{
  // Type-check configuration, and the two-config split every package under
  // `packages/` uses (feature 080, T042 / R11). `tsconfig.base.json`'s `paths`
  // block is active here, so `@endora-commerce/contracts` resolves at its
  // *source* and this package type-checks against the branch it is on (issue
  // #255). `noEmit` is set for that reason: with `paths` active an emit would
  // land beside another package's source. The emitting configuration is
  // `tsconfig.build.json`.
  //
  // This package carries an `endora` block in **no** form, deliberately: that
  // block is how the workspace tells a member the running platform *composes*
  // from a library one, and `backend/test/unit/harness/workspace-resolution.test.ts`
  // reads it in both directions — a member declaring one is refused a
  // `tsconfig.base.json` `paths` entry, a member without one is required to have
  // both. The CLI is composed by nobody, so it takes the entries.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": "./dist",
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  // `test/` is named here and its `*.test.ts` files are **not** excluded: an
  // exclusion written in the type-check half is a test no `tsc` invocation
  // reads. It stood here until 2026-09-07, so this package's twelve test files
  // were in no type-check program at all while `include` said otherwise — the
  // same end state `packages/contracts` reached by narrowing `include` instead.
  // The exclusion the emit needs lives in `tsconfig.build.json`, which is where
  // `backend/test/unit/packages/package-dist-build.test.ts` reads it.
  "include": ["src/**/*", "test/**/*"]
}
